    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yelu-dashi">Yelü Dashi</a> fled the Jin conquest of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/liao-dynasty">Liao</a> in 1124 with the 20,000 troops of the Kedun garrison, took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/balasagun">Balasaghun</a> in 1134 and made the Kingdom of Qocho, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karluks">Karluks</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kara-khanid-khanate">Karakhanids</a> his <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassals</a>.</li><li>At the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-qatwan">Battle of Qatwan</a> on 9 September 1141 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khitans">Khitans</a> encircled and destroyed the Seljuk army of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ahmad-sanjar">Ahmad Sanjar</a> north of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samarkand">Samarkand</a>, winning all of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/transoxiana">Transoxiana</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khwarazm">Khwarazm</a>'s tribute.</li><li>The state called itself the Great <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/liao-dynasty">Liao</a>, kept the Chinese calendar, titles, coins and seals, and was ruled by two empresses in its own right, Xiao Tabuyan and Yelü Pusuwan.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>In 1146 a Jin envoy refused to dismount before the regent Xiao Tabuyan and demanded she bow to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/son-of-heaven">Son of Heaven</a>; she had him executed, and the Jin learned his fate only in 1175 from deserters.</p></aside>
    </section>

